_src":2371232},{"file":"mosque_tunis_lod1.glb","tris":14768,"bytes":533036,"bytes_src":1477584},{"file":"mosque_tunis_lod2.glb","tris":7008,"bytes":267768,"bytes_src":844316}],"materials":["ashlar_limestone","cast_iron","darj_panel","decals","decals_dz","door_planks","fieldstone","glass_dirty","limewash_worn","palm_frond_dz","patio_flags","plaster_rough","roof_slate","sandstone_ochre","screed_lime","steel_galv","timber_beam","timber_grey","wood_paint"],"theater":"desert","snow":false,"nodes":["main","decals","door_main","door_minaret"],"vertex_colors":"COLOR_0 ubyte (grime x base colour; alpha = decal opacity)","revision":"desert rework 2 (2026-09-26)","rework":{"asset":"now ONE complete landmark (hall + courtyard + minaret, 27.9k tris / 2.2 MB); hall arches open onto a modelled hypostyle (mats, rugs, marble columns + inner arcade, painted joist ceiling, lamps) - near-black 9.3% -> ~0%; green-glazed nave gable, skylights, entry dome, repairs on the hall roof; ochre ashlar dome base + octagonal drum with blind arcades and a two-tone voussoir band; 3 m dome with 16 raised limestone ribs + brass jamour; galleries with paved floors, plank ceilings, blind-arch niches, benches; patio flags, basin water; portal with darj-wa-ktaf spandrel; high windows as grilles over dim reveals","common":"new desert lib materials with real albedo breakup (limewash_worn, mud_render, mudbrick, sandstone_ochre, screed_roof, bitumen_felt, corrugated_galv, patio_flags, palm_log, canvas_camo, darj_panel); decal atlas feathered (no hard quads); interior_dark cards replaced by dim plaster / modelled interiors; AO atlas background dilated (no black mip bleed); warm sand-bounce vertex tint on sun-averted faces; KHR_mesh_quantization (normals/tangents int8, uv1 u16); effective-albedo floor (material lum >= 0.045 linear, material x vertex-colour >= 0.03) and opacity caps on near-black decals (soot 0.5, crack 0.7) so iron, tar, char, scorch and crude never render as pure-black voids; LOD2 re-tuned to ~12-15% of LOD0"},"rework2":{"asset":"LOD2 intact (courtyard, front walls, minaret); hypostyle seen through the arches: first column row + impost beam, flag floor with reed mats (no red/brown rug panels); green nave gable removed and the dome base + drum raised 0.6 m so the drum reads at game zoom; lime roof bay ridges + patchy screed break up the hall roof; warm bounce in shade.","common":"LOD1/LOD2 rebuilt with a shape-preserving per-part reducer (lodfix.py): planar dissolve per part delimited by material, UV seams and vertex-colour bands; only curved parts are collapse-decimated, each on its own with a size-aware floor; no joined-mesh collapse, so walls, courtyards, minaret shafts and tanks keep their shape (no holes, sliver fans or UV smears). LOD2 drops sub-pixel parts (wire, ladders, rope). Weathering decals use a soft desert atlas (decals_dz: 2 variants per kind, random mirror, feathered, no hard quads); roof patches are soft stains plus one feathered relief repair; render loss shows rubble (never orange brick) with a 3.5 cm broken edge. New shared CC0 materials: mud_render2 (Poly Haven dirt_floor, darker/redder than the sand, 2x the fine detail), screed_lime (grey_plaster_02, no craze pattern), limewash_lumpy (medieval_wall_01), corrugated_zinc (corrugated_iron_02), palm_frond_dz (alpha-tested frond / reed-mat atlas, own work). Stronger warm ground bounce in shade (limewash no longer turns blue). Water jars are lathe-turned buff clay (belly, neck, lugs); sandbags are individual pillow bags (squash, sag, pinched tied ends, random bond); sand drifts are low wind ramps feathering into the ground; debris mounds have a soft toe (no rim)."},"gltf_extensions_required":["KHR_mesh_quantization"],"group":"desert"}